      "id": "sol.amc-8-1989-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Pair the terms so each pair sums to \\(50\\): \\(1 + 49,\\) \\(11 + 39,\\) \\(21 + 29,\\) \\(31 + 19,\\) and \\(41 + 9.\\)\n\nThere are \\(5\\) such pairs, so the total is \\(5 \\times 50 = 250.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E .",
      "hints": [
        "Look for pairs of terms that combine into round numbers",
        "Pairing \\(1\\) with \\(49,\\) \\(11\\) with \\(39,\\) and so on, each pair sums to \\(50\\)"
